course: dictionary
lesson: 13158
title: Format: the way something is set out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A format is the way something is arranged, set out or organised. When you write a letter, the format shows where the address, the date and the message go. «Please write your letter in the format we showed in class.» Here format means the layout, the set-out pattern.
explain: Format can also mean the type of a computer file. «Save the photo in JPEG format so everyone can open it.» The format is the kind of file, not the picture itself. As a verb, format can mean to prepare something: «Dad will format the memory card» means he will get it ready, and that wipes everything off it.
explain: The words around a word give the clue. «The sports day format is three races and a relay.» Here format means the plan or rules of the event. Ask yourself: is this about how something is set out, what type of file it is, or what the rules are? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A format is the layout, or way something is set out, such as a letter or a book.
fact: «File format» means the type of a computer file, such as JPEG or PDF.
fact: «Formatting» text, such as making it bold or adding a heading, changes how it looks.
fact: Formatting a memory card wipes everything on it, so check before you do it.
exercise: «Write your letter in the correct format, with the address at the top.» What does format mean here? | To wipe something clean | *The layout, or way the letter is set out | A game with winners and losers | A type of computer file
exercise: «Save the photo in PNG format.» What does format mean in this sentence? | The name of the photo | The person who took the photo | *The type of file | The size of the picture in centimetres
exercise: «The sports day format is three races and a relay.» What does format mean here? | A kind of camera | A pair of trainers | *The plan or rules of the event | Wet grass on the field
test: Mia says, «I will format my memory card tonight.» What will happen to the files on it? | They will be moved to a new folder | *They will be wiped off the card | They will be printed out | Nothing, it will just look neater
test: «Ben formatted the title in bold and added a heading.» What did Ben do? | He sent the title to a friend | He printed the title twice | *He changed how the title looks, with bold and a heading | He deleted the title
exam: Which sentence uses format to mean a type of file? | «Please format your essay with double spacing.» | «We will format the game plan on Monday.» | *«The video is saved in MP4 format, so it plays on most devices.» | «The format of the race was fair.»
